Feature: Creation and population of activity_final_log table in purgo_playground schema based on Final Act Log mapping specification

  Background:
    Given the source tables entity_activity_log and priority_weight_settings exist in purgo_playground schema
    And the target table activity_final_log exists in purgo_playground schema with columns:
      | id              | bigint         | not null   |
      | name            | string         | not null   |
      | created_at      | timestamp      | not null   |
      | value           | double         | not null   |
      | decimal_value   | decimal(10,5)  | not null   |
      | nullable_string | string         | nullable   |
      | special_char_string | string     | nullable   |
    And the mapping specification for activity_final_log requires columns:
      | usr_id          | string         | not null   |
      | usr_name        | string         | not null   |
      | date            | date           | not null   |
      | activity_bucket | string         | not null   |
      | new_act_flag    | string         | not null   |
    And the mapping logic is as follows:
      | Only include records where activity_closed_at >= '2025-01-01' and activity_closed_at is not NULL |
      | Only include records where activity_subcategory = 'Task'                                        |
      | Only include records where modified_by_user_role = 'PN'                                         |
      | Only include records where interaction_type IN ('C&R', 'PF')                                    |
      | activity_bucket is populated by left joining entity_activity_log.subject = priority_weight_settings.task_category and selecting priority_level_desc |
      | new_act_flag is populated as: if cutoff_timestamp is NULL then 'New', else if activity_closed_at <= cutoff_timestamp then 'New', else 'Continuing' |
    And the activity_final_log_errors table exists for error logging with columns:
      | usr_id          | string         | nullable   |
      | usr_name        | string         | nullable   |
      | date            | string         | nullable   |
      | activity_bucket | string         | nullable   |
      | new_act_flag    | string         | nullable   |
      | error_message   | string         | nullable   |
      | error_timestamp | timestamp      | nullable   |

  Scenario: Happy path - Successful population of activity_final_log with valid records
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "A123"              | "John Doe"            | 2025-01-15        | 2025-01-10 12:00:00   | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
      | "B456"              | "Jane Smith"          | 2025-02-01        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "PF"            | "Billing"    |
    And priority_weight_settings contains records:
      | task_category | priority_level_desc |
      | "Support"     | "High"              |
      | "Billing"     | "Medium"            |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag |
      | "A123" | "John Doe" | 2025-01-15  | "High"         | "New"        |
      | "B456" | "Jane Smith"| 2025-02-01 | "Medium"       | "New"        |
    And no records should be inserted into activity_final_log_errors

  Scenario: Error path - Exclude records with activity_closed_at before Jan 2025 or NULL
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "C789"              | "Alice Lee"           | 2024-12-31        | 2025-01-01 09:00:00   | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
      | "D012"              | "Bob Ray"             | NULL              | 2025-01-01 09:00:00   | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "PF"            | "Billing"    |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id "C789" or "D012"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "C789" | "Alice Lee"| 2024-12-31  | "High"         | "New"        | "activity_closed_at before Jan 2025"           | <current_timestamp> |
      | "D012" | "Bob Ray"  | NULL        | "Medium"       | "New"        | "activity_closed_at is NULL"                   | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Exclude records with activity_subcategory not equal to 'Task'
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "E345"              | "Carol King"          | 2025-01-20        | 2025-01-19 10:00:00   | "Call"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id "E345"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "E345" | "Carol King"| 2025-01-20 | "High"         | "New"        | "activity_subcategory not 'Task'"              | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Exclude records with modified_by_user_role not equal to 'PN'
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "F678"              | "Dan Fox"             | 2025-01-25        | 2025-01-24 08:00:00   | "Task"              | "Admin"              | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id "F678"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "F678" | "Dan Fox"  | 2025-01-25  | "High"         | "New"        | "modified_by_user_role not 'PN'"               | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Exclude records with interaction_type not in ('C&R', 'PF')
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "G901"              | "Eve Moss"            | 2025-01-30        | 2025-01-29 07:00:00   | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "Email"         | "Support"    |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id "G901"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "G901" | "Eve Moss" | 2025-01-30  | "High"         | "New"        | "interaction_type not in ('C&R', 'PF')"        | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario Outline: Data-driven test for new_act_flag population logic
    Given entity_activity_log contains a record:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | <usr_id>            | <usr_name>            | <activity_closed_at>| <cutoff_timestamp>   | "Task"              | "PN"                 | <interaction_type>| <subject>   |
    And priority_weight_settings contains a record:
      | task_category | priority_level_desc |
      | <subject>     | <priority_level_desc> |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should contain a record:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag |
      | <usr_id> | <usr_name> | <activity_closed_at> | <priority_level_desc> | <expected_new_act_flag> |

    Examples:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | interaction_type | subject   | priority_level_desc | expected_new_act_flag |
      | "H234" | "Frank Wu" | 2025-02-10        | NULL                 | "C&R"           | "Support" | "High"              | "New"                |
      | "I567" | "Grace Lin"| 2025-02-15        | 2025-02-16 12:00:00  | "PF"            | "Billing" | "Medium"            | "New"                |
      | "J890" | "Henry Kim"| 2025-02-20        | 2025-02-19 12:00:00  | "C&R"           | "Support" | "High"              | "Continuing"         |

  Scenario: Error path - Log error when priority_weight_settings join does not find a match
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "K123"              | "Ivy Chen"            | 2025-03-01        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Unknown"    |
    And priority_weight_settings does not contain a record with task_category = "Unknown"
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id "K123"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "K123" | "Ivy Chen" | 2025-03-01  | NULL            | "New"        | "No matching priority_level_desc for subject"  | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Log error when required source columns are NULL
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | NULL                | "Jack Lee"            | 2025-03-05        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
      | "L456"              | NULL                  | 2025-03-06        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "PF"            | "Billing"    |
    And priority_weight_settings contains records:
      | task_category | priority_level_desc |
      | "Support"     | "High"              |
      | "Billing"     | "Medium"            |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then activity_final_log should not contain records for usr_id NULL or "L456"
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain records:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | NULL   | "Jack Lee" | 2025-03-05  | "High"         | "New"        | "modified_by_user_id is NULL"                  | <current_timestamp> |
      | "L456" | NULL       | 2025-03-06  | "Medium"       | "New"        | "modified_by_user_name is NULL"                | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Log error when duplicate usr_id, usr_name, date combinations are found
    Given entity_activity_log contains records:
      | modified_by_user_id | modified_by_user_name | activity_closed_at | cutoff_timestamp      | activity_subcategory | modified_by_user_role | interaction_type | subject      |
      | "M789"              | "Liam Park"           | 2025-04-01        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
      | "M789"              | "Liam Park"           | 2025-04-01        | NULL                  | "Task"              | "PN"                 | "C&R"           | "Support"    |
    And priority_weight_settings contains records:
      | task_category | priority_level_desc |
      | "Support"     | "High"              |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then only one record for usr_id "M789", usr_name "Liam Park", date "2025-04-01" should be inserted into activity_final_log
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain a record:
      | usr_id | usr_name   | date        | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | "M789" | "Liam Park"| 2025-04-01  | "High"         | "New"        | "Duplicate usr_id, usr_name, date combination" | <current_timestamp> |

  Scenario: Error path - Log error when mapping specification columns are missing in activity_final_log table definition
    Given the activity_final_log table does not contain columns:
      | usr_id          |
      | usr_name        |
      | date            |
      | activity_bucket |
      | new_act_flag    |
    When the Databricks SQL script is executed to populate activity_final_log
    Then no records should be inserted into activity_final_log
    And activity_final_log_errors should contain a record:
      | usr_id | usr_name | date | activity_bucket | new_act_flag | error_message                                 | error_timestamp      |
      | NULL   | NULL     | NULL | NULL           | NULL         | "Target table missing required columns"        | <current_timestamp> |
